      "repair_reason": "- [P1] This needs maintainer/security-boundary review and current-head proof rather than ClawSweeper repair because the code intentionally tightens reusable exec approvals.; Cleared: The diff touches a security-sensitive process-exec approval boundary but appears to tighten authorization and does not add dependencies, secrets handling, workflow permissions, or supply-chain execution paths. (sha=71bfe806a598f8bf78e85989414a4645942af5d4)",
      "review_summary": "The branch adds shared package-manager exec parsing and uses it to retarget durable exec approval matching, allow-always persistence, and node-host mutable operand binding for npm, pnpm, and yarn exec-style wrappers.\n\nPR surface: Source +322, Tests +922. Total +1244 across 10 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. Current main lacks the shared package-manager trust-target parser and the PR’s added source tests show the stale-wrapper and inner-executable paths, though I did not run the tests in this read-only review.",
